    "c1": {
      "type": "muto-chapter",
      "settings": {
        "anchor": "what-changes",
        "number": "01",
        "label": "What changes after 35",
        "heading": "Somewhere after 35, your body starts working a little differently.",
        "intro": "<p>Nothing dramatic happens overnight. But three quiet shifts start inside your 30 trillion cells, and they build through your 40s and 50s.</p>",
        "art": "decline",
        "takeaway": "It’s not you doing anything wrong. It’s biology, and the basics you took at 30 weren’t built for it.",
        "line": "",
        "small": "",
        "cta_label": "",
        "cta_link": "",
        "tint": false,
        "space_top": 96,
        "space_bottom": 96,
        "art_beside": true
      },
      "blocks": {
        "a": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "title": "You make less NAD+",
            "text": "<p>Every cell makes its own energy, in tiny power stations called mitochondria. NAD+ is the courier that carries energy from your food to them, over and over, all day. From your mid-30s, your body makes less of it. Fewer couriers, the same amount of work.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "title": "You get less back",
            "text": "<p>Your body responds less to the same food and the same training. It’s called anabolic resistance, and it’s what I spent years studying in the lab. Same effort, smaller return.</p>"
          }
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Your cells’ maintenance slows",
            "text": "<p>Making energy creates a little “exhaust”. The crews that clean it up, a family of enzymes called sirtuins, also run on NAD+. Fewer couriers means more competition for the same supply.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "a",
        "b",
        "c"
      ]
    },
    "c2": {
      "type": "muto-chapter",
      "settings": {
        "anchor": "how-it-shows-up",
        "number": "02",
        "label": "How it shows up",
        "heading": "You don’t feel your cells. You feel your day.",
        "intro": "",
        "art": "none",
        "takeaway": "",
        "line": "<p>It’s like your body has switched to low power mode. Still working, still getting through the day, but running on less than it used to.</p>",
        "small": "",
        "cta_label": "",
        "cta_link": "",
        "tint": false,
        "space_top": 96,
        "space_bottom": 96,
        "band": "dark"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Sharp at 8am. Gone by 3pm."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Hard sessions hang around for days."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "text": "I’m doing everything right, and I still feel it."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "q1",
        "q2",
        "q3"
      ]
    },
    "c3": {
      "type": "muto-chapter",
      "settings": {
        "anchor": "whats-in-it",
        "number": "03",
        "label": "What’s in it",
        "heading": "Five jobs, one jar.",
        "intro": "<p>MUTO is built for what you actually need after 35: one daily formula covering five jobs, so you’re not guessing across five separate pots.</p>",
        "art": "none",
        "takeaway": "",
        "line": "",
        "small": "<p>Vitamins B6 and B12 contribute to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue. Vitamin D contributes to normal muscle function. Vitamins D and K contribute to the maintenance of normal bones. Zinc, copper and vitamin D contribute to the normal function of the immune system. In a study of adults aged 40 to 60, 300mg of NR a day raised NAD+ by 51% in two weeks. That study tested NR on its own, not MUTO.</p>",
        "cta_label": "See every ingredient",
        "cta_link": "/pages/ingredients",
        "tint": false,
        "space_top": 96,
        "space_bottom": 96
      },
